          %h2#Models Models
          %p There are various different models for describing and constructing fiber integration in K-theory.
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InTermsOfBundlesOfFredholmOperators"} In terms of bundles of Fredholm operators
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#InOperatorKKTheory"} In operator KK-theory
          %h3#InTermsOfBundlesOfFredholmOperators In terms of bundles of Fredholm operators
          %p
            We discuss here fiber integration in the model of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "twisted%20K-theory#ByBundlesOfFredholmOperators"} by bundles of spaces of Fredholm operators
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "CareyWang05"} Carey-Wang 05
          %ol
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#AlongAFibrationOfClosedSpinCManifolds"} Along a fibration of closed spin^c manifolds
          %h4#along_a_fibration_of_closed_manifolds
            Along a fibration of closed
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Spin
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^c
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon Y \longrightarrow X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+manifolds"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            carrying fiberwise a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structure"} spin^c structure
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            write
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_x
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                over
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_x \to Y_x
                for the fiberwise
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec"} spin^c
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi x
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi P
                        %mi x
                      %munder
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Spin
                            %mi c
                      %msub
                        %mi Cl
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(Y)_x \coloneqq P_x \underset{Spin^c}{\times} Cl_n
                for the fiberwise
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+bundle"} Clifford bundle
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_x
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec"} spin^c
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+bundle"} spin bundle
                on
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_x
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_x\colon \Gamma(S_x)\to \Gamma(S_x)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%5Ec+Dirac+operator"} Spin^c Dirac operator
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+sections"} space of sections
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinors"} spinors
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mi x
                      %mo ≔
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi D
                            %mi x
                        %msqrt
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo +
                            %msubsup
                              %mi D
                              %mi x
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mi x
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde D_x \coloneqq \frac{D_x}{\sqrt{1+ D_x^\ast D_x}} \colon L^2(S_x)\to L^2(S_x)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+linear+operator"} bounded
                version;
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_x
            depends smoothly on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            while
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde D_x
            still depends continuously on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CL
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CL(Y)_y
            with the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cl
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl_n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            given on elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi Cl
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in \mathbb{R}^n \hookrightarrow Cl_n
            joint right Clifford product by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            and left Clifford product by the volume element
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi vol
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi v
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  vol \cdot (-) \cdot v
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_x
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+commutator"} graded-commutes
            with this
            = succeed "-action." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cl
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl_n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto \tilde D_x
            defines a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi Fred
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tilde D_{(-)} \colon X \longrightarrow Fred^{(n)}
          %p
            from the base to the space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operators"} Fredholm operators
            %span.newWikiWord
              graded-commuting
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/graded-commutator"} ?
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cl
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl_n
            %a{:href => "twisted%20K-theory#ByBundlesOfFredholmOperators"} here
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
          %p
            More generally, let then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to Y
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            representing a class in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^0(Y)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection"} connection
            this twists the above constrction to yield
            = succeed "-twisted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi x
                    %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde D^V_x
            and hence a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mover
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi Fred
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tilde D_{(-)}^V \colon X \longrightarrow Fred^{(n)}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This represents the push-forward class in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mrow
                        %mi dim
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{dim(Y_x)}(X)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\int f
                  \\colon
                  K^0(Y) \longrightarrow K^{dim(Y)-dim()X}(X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim(Y_x)
            even and hence ignoring the compatibility with the
            = succeed "-action," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cl
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl_n
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "CareyWang05"} Carey-Wang 05
          %h3#InOperatorKKTheory In operator KK-theory
          %p
            We discuss fiber integration /push-forward/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Umkehr+maps"}> Umkehr maps
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gysin+maps"} Gysin maps
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#ConnesSkandalis84"}> Connes-Skandalis 85
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BMRS07"} BMRS 07, section 3
          %p The following discusses KK-pushforward
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#KKPushForwardAlongEmbedding"} Along an embedding
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#KKPushforwardAlongSubmersion"} Along a submersion
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#AlongAFibrationOfClosedSpinCManifolds"} Along a fibration of closed spin^c manifolds
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#KKPushforwardAlongGeneralMap"} Along a general K-oriented map
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#KKPushforwardAlongGeneralMap"} In twisted K-theory
          %p
            The construction goes back to (
            %a{:href => "#Connes82"}> Connes 82
            ), where it is given over smooth manifolds. Then (
            %a{:href => "#ConnesSkandalis84"}> Connes-Skandalis 84
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#HilsumSkandalis87"} Hilsum-Skandalis 87
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliations"} foliations
            by KK-elements betwen the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+convolution+algebras"} groupoid convolution algebras
            of the coresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy+groupoids"} holonomy groupoids
            and (
            %a{:href => "#RouseWang10"}> Rouse-Wang 10
            ) further generalize to the case where a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle"} circle 2-bundle
            twist is present over these foliations. A purely algebraic generalization to (K-oriented) maps between otherwise arbitrary
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+topology"} noncommutative spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#BMRS07"}> BMRS 07
            ).
          %h4#KKPushForwardAlongEmbedding Along an embedding
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "ConnesSkandalis84"}> Connes-Skandalis 84, above prop. 2.8
            )
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \colon X \hookrightarrow Y
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
          %p
            The push-forward constructed from this is supposed to be an element in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi KK
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h! \colon KK_d(C(X), C(Y))
          %p
            in terms of which the push-forward on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            is induced by postcomposition:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mo !
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi KK
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo !
                      %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi KK
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi KK
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h_!
                  \\;\colon\;
                  K^\bullet(X)
                  \\simeq
                  KK_\bullet(\mathbb{C}, X)
                  \\stackrel{h!\circ (-)}{\to}
                  KK_{\bullet+d}(\mathbb{C},Y)
                  \\simeq
                  KK^{\bullet+d}(Y)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = dim(X) - dim(Y)
          %p
            Now, if we could “thicken”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a bit, namely to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighbourhood"} tubular neighbourhood
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi U
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi j
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h  \;\colon\; X \hookrightarrow U \stackrel{j}{\hookrightarrow} Y
          %p
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(X)
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            without changing the K-theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo !
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi KK
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  j! \in KK(C_0(U), C(Y))
          %p
            induced directly from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0(U) \to C(Y)
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishing at infinity
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            to functions on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi KK
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi \colon C(X) \stackrel{\simeq_{KK}}{\to} C_0(U)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The bulk of the technical work in constructing the push-forward is in constructing this equivalence. (
            %a{:href => "#BMRS07"}> BMRS 07, example 3.3
            )
          %p
            In order for it to exist at all, assume that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N_Y X \coloneqq h^\ast(T Y)/ T X
          %p
            has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structure"} spin^c structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S(N_Y X)
            for the associated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundle"} spinor bundle
          %p
            Then there is an invertible element in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ι
                    %mi X
                  %mo !
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi KK
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\iota^X! \in KK_n(C(X), C_0(N_Y X))
          %p
            hence a KK-equivalence
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ι
                      %mi X
                    %mo !
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi Y
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota^X! \colon C(X) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} C_0(N_Y X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0(-)
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vanishing+at+infinity"} vanishing at infinity
          %p
            This is defined as follows. Consider the pullback
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                    %mo *
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n^\ast S(N_Y X) \to N_Y X
            of this spinor to the normal bundle itself along the projection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi N
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi Y
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_N \colon N_Y X \to X
          %p
            Moreover, a choice of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            allows to find a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighbourhood"} tubular neighbourhood
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{h(X)}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(X)
            and a neighbourhood of the zero-section of of the normal bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Phi \colon U_{h(X)} \hookrightarrow N_Y X
                  \\,.
          %p This induces a KK-equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi KK
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\Phi] \colon C_0(N_Y X) \stackrel{\simeq_{KK}}{\to} C_0(U)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Therefore the push-forward in operator K-theory along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \hookrightarrow Y
            is given by postcomposing in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi KK
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mi X
                      %mo !
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi KK
                    %mi Φ
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo !
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  h! \colon
                  C(X)
                  \\underoverset{\simeq_{KK}}{i^X!}{\to}
                  C_0(N_Y X)
                  \\underoverset{\simeq_{KK}}{\Phi}{\to}
                  C_0(U)
                  \\stackrel{j!}{\to}
                  C(Y)
                  \\,.
          %h4#KKPushforwardAlongSubmersion Along a proper submersion
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "ConnesSkandalis84"}> Connes-Skandalis 84, above prop. 2.9
            )
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon X \to Z
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-orientation"} K-oriented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+map"} proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submersion"} submersion
            of compact smooth manifolds, the push-forward map along it is reduced to the
            %a{:href => "#KKPushForwardAlongEmbedding"} above
            case of an embedding by
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                using that by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney+embedding+theorem"} Whitney embedding theorem
                every compact
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                may be embedded into some
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{2q}
                such as to yield an embedding
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      h \colon X \to Z \times \mathbb{R}^{2 q}
            %li
              %p using that there is a KK-equivalence
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ι
                        %mi Z
                      %mo !
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi KK
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\iota^Z! \colon C(Z) \stackrel{\simeq_{KK}}{\to} C_0(Z \times \mathbb{R}^{2q})
                      \\,.
          %p
            The resulting push-forward is then given by postcomposition in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo !
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi KK
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ι
                        %mi Z
                      %mo !
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi! \colon C(X) \stackrel{h!}{\to} C_0(Z \times \mathbb{R}^{2}q)
                  \\underoverset{\simeq_{KK}}{(\iota^Z!)^{-1}}{\to}
                  C(Z)
                  \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BMRS07"}> BMRS 07, example 3.4
            )
          %h4#AlongAFibrationOfClosedSpinCManifolds
            Along a smooth fibration of closed
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Spin
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin^c
          %p
            Specifically, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon X \to Z
            a smooth fibration over a closed smooth manifold whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/Z
            are
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structure"} spin^c
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
              of even
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
          %p
            the push-forward element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo !
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi KK
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi! \in KK(C_0(X), C_0(Z))
            is given by the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+module"} Fredholm
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+module"} Hilbert module
            obatined from the fiberwise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+Dirac+operator"} spin^c Dirac operator
            acting on the fiberwise
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinors"} spinors
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "ConnesSkandalis84"} Connes-Skandalis 84, proof of lemma 4.7
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "BMRS07"} BMRS 07, example 3.9
          %p In detail, write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  T(X/Z) \hookrightarrow T X
          %p
            for the sub-bundle of the total
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+vectors"} vertical vectors
            and choose a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^{X/Z}
            on this bundle (hence a collection of Riemannian metric on the fibers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/Z
            smoothly varying along
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{X/Z}
            for the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundle"} spinor bundle
          %p
            A choice of horizontal complenet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi H
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \simeq T^H X \oplus T(X/Z)
            induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+connection"} affine connection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∇
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla^{X/Z}
            = succeed "/Clifford" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symbol+map"} symbol map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^\ast (X/Z)
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{X/Z}
            induces a fiberwise
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+Dirac+operator"} spin^c Dirac operator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^2(X/Z, S_{X/Z})
          %p
            This yields a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+module"} Fredholm
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+bimodule"} Hilbert bimodule
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (D_{X/Z}, L^2(X/Z, S_{X/Z}))
          %p
            which defines an element in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo !
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi KK
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi ! \in KK(C_0(X), C_0(Z))
                  \\,.
          %p
            Postcompositon with this is the push-forward map in K/KK-theory, equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
            map of the collection of Dirac operators.
          %h4{:id => "#KKPushforwardAlongGeneralMap"} Along a general K-oriented map
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "ConnesSkandalis84"}> Connes-Skandalis 84, def. 2.1
            )
          %p
            Now for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            an arbitray
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-orientation"} K-oriented
            smooth proper map, we may reduce push-forward along it to the above two cases by factoring it through its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+map"} graph map
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi graph
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mi Y
                  %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f \;\colon\;
                  X \stackrel{graph(f)}{\to}
                  X \times Y
                  \\stackrel{p_Y}{\to}
                  Y
                  \\,.
          %p
            Hence push-forward along such a general map is postcomposition in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            with
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo !
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi Y
                  %mo !
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi graph
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo !
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f! \coloneqq p_Y !\circ graph(f)!
                  \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BMRS07"}> BMRS 07, example 3.5
            )
          %h4#KKPushforwardAlongGeneralMap In twisted K-theory
          %p
            We discuss push forward in K-theory more generally by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality+C%2A-algebras"} Poincaré duality C*-algebras
            hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+objects"} dual objects
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Q
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Q \to X
            be a map of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi \colon X \to B^2 U(1)
            modulate a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-bundle"} circle 2-bundle
            regarded as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twist for K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+groupoid+convolution+algebras"} twisted groupoid convolution algebras
            yields a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            morphism of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟵
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_{i^\ast \chi}(Q)
                  \\stackrel{i^\ast}{\longleftarrow}
                  C_{\chi}(X)
                  \\,,
          %p
            with notation as in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Poincar&#233;+duality+algebra#CStarAlgebraOf2BundleOnManifold"} this definition
            %a{:href => "Poincar&#233;+duality+algebra#DualOfCompactManifoldWithTwist"} this proposition
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+morphism"} dual morphism
            is of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                        %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_{\frac{W_3(\tau_Q)}{i^\ast \chi}}(Q)
                  \\stackrel{i_!}{\longrightarrow}
                  C_{\frac{W_3(\tau_X)}{\chi}}(X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            If we assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structure"} spin^c structure
            then this is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                        %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mo !
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_{\frac{W_3(\tau_Q)}{i^\ast \chi}}(Q)
                  \\stackrel{i_!}{\longrightarrow}
                  C_{\frac{1}{\chi}}(X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Postcomposition with this map in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            now yields a map from the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi i
                          %mo *
                        %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{W_3(\tau_Q)}{i^\ast \chi}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            to the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi χ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi^{-1}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi χ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i_! \colon K_{\bullet + W_3(\tau_Q) - i^\ast \chi}(Q) \to K_{\bullet -\chi}
                  \\,.
          %p
            If we here think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Q
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Q \hookrightarrow X
            as being the inclusion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            would be the class of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            and an element
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi τ
                        %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %msup
                        %mi i
                        %mo *
                      %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\xi] \in K_{\bullet + W_3(\tau_Q) - i^\ast \chi}(Q)
          %p
            is called (the K-class of) a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton gauge field
            on the D-brane satisfying the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten-Kapustin+anomaly+cancellation"} Freed-Witten-Kapustin anomaly cancellation
            mechanism. (The orginal
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten+anomaly+cancellation"} Freed-Witten anomaly cancellation
            assumes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
            given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+unitary+bundle"} twisted line bundle
            in which case it exhibits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+spin%5Ec+structure"} twisted spin^c structure
            on
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"} push-forward
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mo !
